    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T02:28:29Z",
    "body": "Back to draft for one change: the built-in Lathe's X band. Facing to centre puts the control point past centreline (X-1.6 for r = 0.8 under orientation 2), which `lathe.mch`'s one-sided X 0..320 would refuse. The contributor's PathPilot Hub 8L conversational facing ends every pass at `G1 X-0.0174` (diameter), so a control's own facing does go past centre. Widening the band slightly negative, overturning `lathe_x_stays_a_centreline_band` with the reason recorded. Will re-flag ready once re-gated.",
