    "body": "Re-flagged ready at 53e4aebb. The built-in Lathe's X band is now -2.5..320 (radius; Ø-5). That overturns the #493 one-sided rule, with the reason recorded in docs/decisions/630-nose-tip.md: the PathPilot Hub 8L facing sample ends every pass at Ø-0.0174 in, past centre, and ours stops at -2r for no pip. New pins in lathe_stroke: `a_facing_pass_to_centre_fits_the_built_in_lathe_x_band` and `a_real_x_overtravel_past_centre_still_refuses_by_name`. Gate: lathe_stroke 7, lathe_nose_tip 6, the lathe_post*, turning_*, machine*, conformance, golden_cl and posting suites all pass; clippy is clean. Found along the way and filed separately: the stroke check reads world X, not the turning radius on the Y meridian ().",
